    "body": "Adds an opt-in, single C++ ROS 2 planner that converts timestamped ball observations and registered robot pose into model-validated, runner-compatible racket commands. It combines our six-state CKF and deterministic incoming prediction with local contact selection, shared-physics outgoing planning, impact reconstruction, and command validation.\n\nThe implementation supports automatic reacquisition after rejection, causal quaternion-derived spin when available, position-only operation when spin is unavailable, and the corrected base-pose orientation contract. The legacy backend remains available.\n\nOutput remains shadow-only. This PR requests review of the planner-to-command contribution\u2014not authorization to actuate the robot or a claim of demonstrated physical return performance.",
